## Shared data semantics

The current account is the tenant boundary. Chatwoot work can involve inboxes, contacts, conversations, messages, human agents,
teams, labels, reports, automations, settings, and Captain assistants and knowledge. A concept existing in Chatwoot does not prove
that it is queryable or writable; inspect the exposed resources and capabilities.

Inboxes receive conversations through communication channels. A contact is a customer profile and can participate in multiple conversations.
A conversation belongs to an account, inbox, and contact. It can have a status, priority, assignee, team, labels, and custom attributes.
Messages form the conversation history. Direction, visibility, sender, delivery state, and quoted history have different meanings.
Human agents can belong to teams and inboxes. Assignment eligibility and current capacity must be established before assignment.
Custom attributes are account-defined JSON. Verify their available keys and meanings from exposed account data; never guess a key from its likely name.

Resources are logical, account-scoped views, not arbitrary database tables. Follow exposed relationships and fields.
Use database IDs for references; display_id is a separate user-facing identifier. Query rows have selected fields, not implicit ref objects.
Enums such as message_type are names (incoming/outgoing), not numeric database codes. Timestamps are ISO 8601 values, not numbers.
Use WootQL now() minus a duration for rolling time windows; use calendar boundaries only when requested.
Rows must be explicitly ordered for sequence processing, with a unique tie-breaker. Pagination can split a conversation's history.
An empty page or zero count is data, not evidence of a broken query. Establish coverage before drawing conclusions.

Null means absent, not empty. Conversation labels are non-null lists; no labels is [], never null or the string "{}".
WootQL is empty means zero characters for text or zero elements for lists; whitespace is not empty.
Both is empty and is not empty yield unknown for null and therefore exclude it in where, even under not.
Use field is null or field is empty to include both. Empty tests reject numeric, boolean, date, and JSON fields.
A missing right-side record in a left join may introduce null even for normally non-null fields; it is not an unlabeled conversation.
In Scheme, nil? tests database null, null? tests an empty list, and only #f is false. These are different values.
